{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CWkDj2epDSxYa4Ka1STziB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 0002 — runtime host shipped (Tier-1 deterministic) (2026-06-22)\n2\t\n3\t> Not an advisor *cycle* but a BUILD entry: the runtime host the first real run (journal/0001) opened as\n4\t> a follow-up is now built. Provenance: genuine-execution build against the frozen plan\n5\t> (`planning/runtime-host/`); validated by `node --test test/*.test.mjs`. cross_model:false (single-family).\n6\t\n7\t## What shipped\n8\t\n9\tThe missing **runtime host** for Gandalf v1 — the thin entry that turns a model's RAW draft into a\n10\tcanary-conformant, honestly-graded advisor output by running the **already-shipped** deterministic seam\n11\tengine. Three artifacts, additive (a new `runtime/` dir + new `test/runtime-*.test.mjs` + a docs touch):\n12\t\n13\t- **`runtime/seam-pass.mjs`** — `applySeamPass(rawDraft, { cross_model = false })`, a PURE composer.\n14\t  By `kind`: diagnose → `stampDiagnoseCoreProvenance`; anticipate → `composeAnticipation`\n15\t  (subject_cardinality:1); situate → `composeSituate`. Only REFUTED drops (`dropsFromOutput`). Each\n16\t  elevation → `vetElevationRefutation` → `labelTier(..., {cross_model})`. `risk_labels` via\n17\t  `composeRiskLabels`. Any per-item `degraded` rolls up to top-level `degraded` (B6). A malformed draft\n18\t  throws the NAMED `SeamPassInputError` — never a fabricated finding, never a partial output.\n19\t- **`runtime/gandalf-run.mjs`** — the real CLI: `--input <file>` | stdin → `applySeamPass` →\n20\t  `assertIncrement1Conformant` → `--output <file>` | stdout. Malformed input / a failed assertion ⇒\n21\t  non-zero exit + honest stderr + NOTHING written.\n22\t- **`runtime/RAW-DRAFT-CONTRACT.md`** — what the model emits in runtime mode: ONLY the raw draft; it does\n23\t  NOT self-assign tiers/stamps — the host applies them.\n24\t\n25\t## Why (closes journal/0001)\n26\t\n27\tThe first real run proved the model produces excellent DIAGNOSE/SITUATE/ANTICIPATE *content* but, run as\n28\tpure SKILL.md prose, keeps hand-approximating the tier stamps and failing B-honesty three ways\n29\t(named-defeater not a structured field → a below-threshold elevation stamped above SPECULATIVE → a\n30\tSPECULATIVE elevation missing the literal \"no independent refutation ran\" stamp). All three are the SAME\n31\troot cause: the honest tiers + stamps are the SEAM's job, applied deterministically — not the model's.\n32\tThe host is that wiring. With it, the output is canary-conformant **by construction**.\n33\t\n34\t## Scope = Tier-1 (deterministic), by design\n35\t\n36\tONE model run, the deterministic seam pass — NO live independent named-defeater refuters and NO\n37\tresearchPrime SITUATE commission (those need the `agent()` seam the repo flags as the integration point\n38\tthe gate never runs). So every **elevation** honestly lands at **SPECULATIVE** carrying the\n39\t`NO_INDEPENDENT_REFUTATION_STAMP`; the **diagnosis** keeps its evidence rung + `gandalf_core`; `risk_labels`\n40\tcap at the single-family **PROMISING** ceiling; only **REFUTED** drops.\n41\t\n42\t## Follow-on (sequenced, NOT in this effort)\n43\t\n44\tThe **live-refuter PROMISING tier** — actually dispatching the independent named-defeater refuter (and the\n45\tresearchPrime SITUATE commission) so an above-threshold elevation can EARN PROMISING — needs the trio\n46\t`agent()` seam, consistent with the Gandalf program's own dependency sequencing. It is OUT of this effort\n47\tand OUT of the gate.\n48\t\n49\t## Sleep gate / canary result\n50\t\n51\t`node --test test/*.test.mjs` GREEN: the existing 130 canary tests held (the host is additive — it\n52\treuses the shipped seams + harness, reimplements no grading logic) PLUS the new runtime tests\n53\t(`runtime-seam-pass` / `runtime-entry` / `runtime-integration`). No drift; the single-family PROMISING\n54\tceiling and the SPECULATIVE refutation floor are applied by the seams, not the host.\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"549832a8-8582-4358-912d-15a5b08fb91d","uuid":"9ca5810f-5933-4f1f-b274-023072d47b35","timestamp":"2026-06-23T19:23:55.072Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\Skill Foundry\\skills\\gandalf\\journal\\0002-runtime-host.md","content":"# 0002 — runtime host shipped (Tier-1 deterministic) (2026-06-22)\n\n> Not an advisor *cycle* but a BUILD entry: the runtime host the first real run (journal/0001) opened as\n> a follow-up is now built. Provenance: genuine-execution build against the frozen plan\n> (`planning/runtime-host/`); validated by `node --test test/*.test.mjs`. cross_model:false (single-family).\n\n## What shipped\n\nThe missing **runtime host** for Gandalf v1 — the thin entry that turns a model's RAW draft into a\ncanary-conformant, honestly-graded advisor output by running the **already-shipped** deterministic seam\nengine. Three artifacts, additive (a new `runtime/` dir + new `test/runtime-*.test.mjs` + a docs touch):\n\n- **`runtime/seam-pass.mjs`** — `applySeamPass(rawDraft, { cross_model = false })`, a PURE composer.\n  By `kind`: diagnose → `stampDiagnoseCoreProvenance`; anticipate → `composeAnticipation`\n  (subject_cardinality:1); situate → `composeSituate`. Only REFUTED drops (`dropsFromOutput`). Each\n  elevation → `vetElevationRefutation` → `labelTier(..., {cross_model})`. `risk_labels` via\n  `composeRiskLabels`. Any per-item `degraded` rolls up to top-level `degraded` (B6). A malformed draft\n  throws the NAMED `SeamPassInputError` — never a fabricated finding, never a partial output.\n- **`runtime/gandalf-run.mjs`** — the real CLI: `--input <file>` | stdin → `applySeamPass` →\n  `assertIncrement1Conformant` → `--output <file>` | stdout. Malformed input / a failed assertion ⇒\n  non-zero exit + honest stderr + NOTHING written.\n- **`runtime/RAW-DRAFT-CONTRACT.md`** — what the model emits in runtime mode: ONLY the raw draft; it does\n  NOT self-assign tiers/stamps — the host applies them.\n\n## Why (closes journal/0001)\n\nThe first real run proved the model produces excellent DIAGNOSE/SITUATE/ANTICIPATE *content* but, run as\npure SKILL.md prose, keeps hand-approximating the tier stamps and failing B-honesty three ways\n(named-defeater not a structured field → a below-threshold elevation stamped above SPECULATIVE → a\nSPECULATIVE elevation missing the literal \"no independent refutation ran\" stamp). All three are the SAME\nroot cause: the honest tiers + stamps are the SEAM's job, applied deterministically — not the model's.\nThe host is that wiring. With it, the output is canary-conformant **by construction**.\n\n## Scope = Tier-1 (deterministic), by design\n\nONE model run, the deterministic seam pass — NO live independent named-defeater refuters and NO\nresearchPrime SITUATE commission (those need the `agent()` seam the repo flags as the integration point\nthe gate never runs). So every **elevation** honestly lands at **SPECULATIVE** carrying the\n`NO_INDEPENDENT_REFUTATION_STAMP`; the **diagnosis** keeps its evidence rung + `gandalf_core`; `risk_labels`\ncap at the single-family **PROMISING** ceiling; only **REFUTED** drops.\n\n## Follow-on (sequenced, NOT in this effort)\n\nThe **live-refuter PROMISING tier** — actually dispatching the independent named-defeater refuter (and the\nresearchPrime SITUATE commission) so an above-threshold elevation can EARN PROMISING — needs the trio\n`agent()` seam, consistent with the Gandalf program's own dependency sequencing. It is OUT of this effort\nand OUT of the gate.\n\n## Sleep gate / canary result\n\n`node --test test/*.test.mjs` GREEN: the existing 130 canary tests held (the host is additive — it\nreuses the shipped seams + harness, reimplements no grading logic) PLUS the new runtime tests\n(`runtime-seam-pass` / `runtime-entry` / `runtime-integration`). No drift; the single-family PROMISING\nceiling and the SPECULATIVE refutation floor are applied by the seams, not the host.\n","numLines":55,"startLine":1,"totalLines":55}}}
